---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/doge.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Local Government Reorganisation in Lancashire | Tom Pickup"
  description="Lancashire's councils are being abolished and rebuilt as four new unitary authorities by April 2028. What that means for your services, your money and the land the public owns, explained plainly."
>
  <div class="doge-page">
    <nav class="doge-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <span class="here">LGR</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="doge-head">
      <span class="doge-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Local Government Reorganisation</span>
      <h1 class="doge-title">Lancashire is being redrawn</h1>
      <p class="doge-sub">
        On 16 July 2026 the government confirmed that Lancashire County Council and the twelve district
        councils will be abolished and replaced by <strong>four new unitary authorities</strong>. Shadow
        elections are in May 2027 and the new councils take over on 1 April 2028. It is the biggest change
        to how Lancashire is run in fifty years. This is where I track what it means, in plain English, for
        your services, your council tax and the land and buildings the public owns.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="doge-grid">
      <a href="/lgr/property/" class="doge-card">
        <span class="doge-card-kicker">Live</span>
        <div class="doge-card-title">Property &amp; land</div>
        <div class="doge-card-desc">
          An interactive, filterable map of publicly owned property and land across all fourteen Lancashire
          councils, sortable by today's borough and by the future unitary that will inherit it.
        </div>
        <span class="doge-card-go">Open the map →</span>
      </a>

      <div class="doge-card disabled">
        <span class="doge-card-kicker">Coming soon</span>
        <div class="doge-card-title">The four new councils</div>
        <div class="doge-card-desc">
          What each new unitary will look like: population, area, the councils it merges and the estate it
          inherits.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doge-card disabled">
        <span class="doge-card-kicker">Coming soon</span>
        <div class="doge-card-title">The cost of change</div>
        <div class="doge-card-desc">
          Set-up costs, claimed savings and who pays. The competing figures, laid out and sourced.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doge-card disabled">
        <span class="doge-card-kicker">Coming soon</span>
        <div class="doge-card-title">Your area</div>
        <div class="doge-card-desc">
          Enter your postcode to see which new unitary you move into and what it will run.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doge-disclaimer">
      <strong>How to read this section.</strong> Reorganisation is set out in law but many of the details,
      names, boundaries, costs and asset transfers, are still being worked through. Where a figure is
      contested I say so and give the source. Nothing here is a council publication; it is my own work as a
      Lancashire county councillor to make the process something residents can actually follow.
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
